<header><h1>Neighbors: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_neighbors">Neighbors</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player may make a deal with any player, however, these deals may only include a transaction if the two players are neighbors.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 28.1: &ldquo;Players can make deals with each other at any time, even if they are not neighbors. However, deals that include a transaction must follow the rules for transactions, including that the players be neighbors.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who can make transactions, and when?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Deals that don&rsquo;t exchange components can be made with anyone at any time.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Some effects allow players who are not neighbors to resolve transactions, such as controlling <a href="/R_space_stations">space stations</a>, the <a href="/R_agenda_phase">agenda phase</a>, the <a href="/F_hacan">Hacan</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Emirates_of_Hacan#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Guild%20Ships"><sc>Guild Ships</sc></a> faction ability, the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Temporal%20Command%20Suite"><i>Temporal Command Suite</i></a> technology and the <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Breakthrough:~:text=Deepgloom%20Executable"><i>Deepgloom Executable</i></a> breakthrough.<sup>1,2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can players make transactions with non-neighbors during the agenda phase?&rdquo;: &ldquo;every pair of players may make one transaction, neighbors or not. That doesn&rsquo;t make them neighbors for anything else.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.6: &ldquo;While resolving each agenda during the agenda phase, a player may perform one transaction with each other player.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 10: &ldquo;A player that controls a space station can resolve transactions with other players that control a space station, even if they are not neighbors.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>A player may resolve one transaction with each other player per each agenda during the agenda phase, however, the agenda phase does not make all players neighbors.<sup>1,2,3,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can players make transactions with non-neighbors during the agenda phase?&rdquo;: &ldquo;every pair of players may make one transaction, neighbors or not. That doesn&rsquo;t make them neighbors for anything else.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 94.6: &ldquo;While resolving each agenda during the agenda phase, a player may perform one transaction with each other player.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;Each player may negotiate up to one transaction with each other player while resolving the vote for each agenda.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (x3n d0g, 01/17/2019): &ldquo;Simply being in the agenda phase does not confer neighbor status to all players.&rdquo; Neighbor clause stated; transaction-per-agenda limit only loosely supported (agenda phase transactions are free, new transactions allowed per new agenda).</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ships that move through a system do not make their owner neighbors with players who have units in or adjacent to that system, as those ships are never in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who counts as my neighbor?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Ships moving through systems don&rsquo;t create neighbors on the way, since they are never in those systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Players in a space combat or ground combat with each other are neighbors, as they both have units in the same system.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who counts as my neighbor?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Players with a unit or controlled planet in the same system or adjacent systems, wormholes included, so two players fighting in a system are neighbors.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 60: &ldquo;Two players are neighbors if they both have a unit or control a planet in the same system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
